# A view of several kinds, whose kind the store reads off the cell, took a typed store only of what is proven to be a number. Of what `from[i]` gives nothing is known:
# it is asked for a number, and the store is the proven one; what is none goes the generic way.
# So in front of a loop that stores what nobody knows, the views that are neither bytes nor doubles nor floats have a copy together.
# RUN(TURNS): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# TURNS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# TURNS: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float32Array #
# TURNS: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Int16Array|Int32Array|Int8Array|Uint16Array|Uint32Array|Uint8ClampedArray #
# TURNS: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=9 level=Proven
# TURNS: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} level=Proven
# TURNS: = ElemSet
# What every turn stores unchanged is asked once in front of that copy, and the store by the kind of the cell is the proven one.
# RUN(UNCHANGED): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# UNCHANGED-LABEL: code f1:Body
# UNCHANGED: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Int16Array|Int32Array|Int8Array|Uint16Array|Uint32Array|Uint8ClampedArray #
# UNCHANGED: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=9 level=Proven
# UNCHANGED: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=number #
# UNCHANGED: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} level=Proven
# UNCHANGED: = ElemSet
